Cross toolchain for flash.tos
=============================

"make" here downloads the sources listed in Makefile (checked against
SHA256SUMS) and builds into install/:

  binutils 2.9.1-mint         assembler of the TOS part, linker and objcopy for all
                              images (a.out); MiNT patches of Frank Naumann
  binutils 2.19.1-mint        assembler of the drivers (ColdFire v4e);
  20091017                    patches/binutils-*-mint-host.patch: build fixes for a
                              current host compiler; both built in docker/
  gcc 3.3.2-mint              C files of the TOS part (boot, pmmu2.c, lz.c, ...);
                              32-bit host only, built in docker/ (needs docker)
  gcc 4.4.2-mint 20091017     drivers; also built as a 32-bit host program in docker/,
                              a 64-bit host build generates different code
  MiNTLib headers             0.57.3 with mint/osbind.h, mint/mintbind.h, compiler.h
                              of 2009-05-22 and mint/sysvars.h of 2010-04-13, the mix
                              the drivers were built with (the code gcc 4.4 generates
                              depends on the number of declarations in the headers);
                              patches/mintlib-2012-compat.patch: "d0" out of the
                              remaining old clobber lists, OSBIND_CLOBBER_LIST in
                              <mint/osbind.h>, <sysvars.h>

bin/ holds the commands the flash.tos Makefiles call:

  tos-gcc       TOS part: gcc 3.3.2 with the binutils 2.9.1 assembler
  drivers-gcc   drivers: gcc 4.4.2 with the binutils 2.19.1 assembler

host/include/ maps the GEMDOS calls of the image tools (gentos, compress) to POSIX.

Build the images:

  make -C gnu
  make -C flash.tos firebee        (flash.tos/firetos_firebee.hex)
  make -C flash.tos ct60           (flash.tos/ctpcitos.bin)

GNU and GNU_PREFIX in the flash.tos Makefiles select another toolchain location.
